+# GRM Mount-Set Curation — Design Draft (lead-authored, 2026-08-30)
+
+Status: DRAFT for David's review. No orders derive from this until the
+ADM1.3 dual-frame verdict lands and David reads this doc. It composes
+the week's receipts into the admission architecture they point at.
+
+## The receipts this design stands on
+
+1. **Co-mount confusion is value blending** (CMC1.1 arms, trued
+   witness): no tie-breaker exists at readout — not outlier energy,
+   not position, not an identifier bonus to δ=0.5. The wrong answer is
+   a chimera; target ~0.2 mass vs siblings ~0.75 diffuse. Ties must be
+   PREVENTED, not broken.
+2. **The router already knows the winner** when one exists: praxis
+   routed rank-1 correctly; modern rank-1 point-lookup structural
+   recall 26/27; the miss rate is real but small (insurance earned —
+   ADM1 verdict REFUTED per rule).
+3. **A-DEC (decisive-admission triage) was never beaten** by any fixed
+   k on any measured class, and its declared-synthesis branch rescued
+   the cross-fact turns fixed k=1 loses (turn-13 receipt).
+4. **Shuttling is proven**: one-mount arena + grounded trips = 6/6,
+   equal to a three-mount arena (foundational receipt).
+5. **L2 lineage-head mounting is admission control with a receipt**
+   (stale 2/5→0/5; now DEFAULT ON) — the pattern generalizes.
+6. **The probe ladder is load-bearing for near-duplicate ANSWER
+   discrimination** (CORPUS-100 16/20→4/20 ladder-off with routing
+   perfect) — curation composes WITH the ladder, never replaces it.
+7. **Self-report is not a demand signal** (S2 FAIL); mechanistic
+   reads are (S1 0.8286, S4 0.756). Demand detection must read state,
+   not testimony.
+
+## The architecture (three stages, one principle)
+
+Principle: **the tie you prevent needs no adjudication; the tie you
+declare is served by the primitive built for it; no tie happens by
+accident.**
+
+### Stage A — Admission triage (per turn, uses only router outputs)
+- Exactly-one identifier-decisive candidate, or rank-1/rank-2 margin
+  above the frozen threshold → **mount the winner alone** (k=1).
+- Two-plus identifier hits → **declared synthesis**: mount the
+  identified set knowingly; tag the arena "confusable set present."
+- Zero identifier hits (ambiguous) → k=3 eager (insurance branch) —
+  note: this class is EMPTY in current certified fixtures; it needs
+  probes before it needs policy.
+- Lineage siblings never co-mount (L2, already default-on).
+
+### Stage B — Serve the declared ties
+For declared-synthesis turns whose members are confusable
+(near-tie topical scores), prefer **shuttle**: serialize the members
+across grounded trips within the turn, compose the answer from
+grounding notes (proven 6/6 pattern). Simultaneous residency only
+when the members are NOT confusable (identifier-distinct).
+
+### Stage C — The demand loop (recover from admission misses)
+The k=1 branch's one-in-27 miss class is repaired, not prevented:
+- **Live-query routing** (primary): score the model's generation-time
+  query fingerprints against the full index continuously; an unmounted
+  graft outranking everything mounted = fetch trigger → trip.
+- **No-good-home signature** (secondary): arena attention mass
+  collapsing to sinks at readout positions (witness machinery,
+  repurposed).
+- **Step-3 identifier audit** (net): probe/response identifiers
+  hitting unmounted grafts → ledgered miss + next-turn repair.
+Registered prediction (lead, pre-data): the detector race will look
+like S1-vs-S2 — mechanistic wins, verbal ask underperforms.
+
+## What ships first (pending ADM1.3 + David)
+
+1. A-DEC behind a default-off flag (wiring plan from ADM1.3; the
+   flip is David's, with the ladder ON — frame receipts required).
+2. Confusable-set tagging at admission (metadata only, zero behavior
+   change — pure telemetry for a shuttle-policy experiment).
+3. The detector-race experiment (Stage C candidates vs planted
+   missing-sibling fixtures) — the S1/S2-shaped receipt.
+4. Shuttle-for-declared-ties experiment on the praxis-class fixture:
+   the direct test that serialization cures blending where admission
+   alone cannot (the query names multiple lookalikes).
+
+## Open questions for David
+
+- Ambiguous-probe corpus: build one (the class is unmeasured — E1-era
+  fixtures never contained vague follow-ups)? Without it the k=3
+  insurance branch is untested policy.
+- Margin threshold governance: frozen constant vs per-model
+  calibration (dialect metadata)?
+- Does Stage C's live-query routing belong in the three-pass
+  architecture as a step-2 monitor, or as trips machinery only?
